{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"role":"article","title":"Using Imported C Functions in Swift","roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Language-Interoperability-with-C-and-C++","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift"],"title":"Language Interoperability with C and C++"}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift imports any function declared in a C header as a Swift global function.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, consider the following C function declarations:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"occ","code":["int product(int multiplier, int multiplicand);","int quotient(int dividend, int divisor, int *remainder);","","struct Point2D createPoint2D(float x, float y);","float distance(struct Point2D from, struct Point2D to);"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here’s how Swift imports them:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func product(_ multiplier: Int32, _ multiplicand: Int32) -> Int32","func quotient(_ dividend: Int32, _ divisor: Int32, _ remainder: UnsafeMutablePointer<Int32>) -> Int32","","func createPoint2D(_ x: Float, _ y: Float) -> Point2D","func distance(_ from: Point2D, _ to: Point2D) -> Float"]},{"level":3,"text":"Use a CVaListPointer to Call Variadic Functions","type":"heading","anchor":"Use-a-CVaListPointer-to-Call-Variadic-Functions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In Swift, you can call C variadic functions, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"vasprintf(_:_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", using the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Swift ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/getVaList(_:)"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/withVaList(_:_:)"},{"text":" functions. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"withVaList(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"function takes an array of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CVarArg"},{"text":" values and provides a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CVaListPointer"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value within the body of a closure parameter, whereas the ","type":"text"},{"code":"getVaList(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns this value directly. With either function, you pass the resulting ","type":"text"},{"code":"CVaListPointer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value as the ","type":"text"},{"code":"va_list","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" argument of the C variadic function.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, here’s how to call the ","type":"text"},{"code":"vasprintf(_:_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function in Swift:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func swiftprintf(format: String, arguments: CVarArg...) -> String? {","    return withVaList(arguments) { va_list in","        var buffer: UnsafeMutablePointer<Int8>? = nil","        return format.withCString { cString in","            guard vasprintf(&buffer, cString, va_list) != 0 else {","                return nil","            }","","            return String(validatingUTF8: buffer!)","        }","    }","}","print(swiftprintf(format: \"√2 ≅ %g\", arguments: sqrt(2.0))!)","\/\/ Prints \"√2 ≅ 1.41421\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift only imports C variadic functions that use a ","type":"text"},{"code":"va_list","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for their arguments.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"C functions that use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"...","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" syntax for variadic arguments are not imported, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"therefore can’t be called using ","type":"text"},{"code":"CVarArg","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" arguments.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Call-Functions-with-Pointer-Parameters","level":3,"text":"Call Functions with Pointer Parameters"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Whenever possible, Swift avoids giving you direct access to pointers. When importing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"C function parameters, however, Swift maps pointer parameters to standard library","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pointer types. The following tables use ","type":"text"},{"code":"Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as a placeholder type name to indicate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"syntax for the mappings.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For return types, variables, and arguments, the following mappings apply:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"C Syntax"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Syntax"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"const Type *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafePointer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"<Type>"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafeMutablePointer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"<Type>"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For class types, the following mappings apply:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"C Syntax"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Syntax"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type * const *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafePointer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"<"},{"type":"text","text":"Type>"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type * __strong *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafeMutablePointer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"<"},{"type":"text","text":"Type>"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Type **"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AutoreleasingUnsafeMutablePointer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"<"},{"type":"text","text":"Type>"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For pointers to untyped, raw memory, the following mappings apply:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"C Syntax"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Syntax"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"const void *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafeRawPointer","isActive":true}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"void *"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/UnsafeMutableRawPointer","isActive":true}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"C function pointers are imported into Swift as closures with the C function pointer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calling convention, denoted by the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@convention(c)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute. For example, a function","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pointer that has the type ","type":"text"},{"code":"int (*)(void)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in C is imported into Swift as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@convention(c) () -> Int32"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the type of the value pointed to by a C pointer cannot be represented by Swift,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as is the case with an incomplete struct type, the pointer is imported as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OpaquePointer"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to call imported functions that are declared in a C header."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how Swift represents imported C structures and unions